                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game says Music-Based Procedural Generation, and it's a giant sack of lies. You can't claim to be procedurally generated, and then ask the user to do all the work, manually calculating the BPM, and setting beat counts. That's not procedural, that's just a metronome and an ipod with generic fighting game over it. Not to mention you have to slog through a chapter of dogwater music tracks before you get to even access this feature. This means that if you're really bad at the game, but want to push through for the music generator, you might pass the 2 hour mark on accident and lose out of your refund. Absolute trash from top to bottom, from the lies about the music feature to the frankly boring gameplay. Immediate refund request.",
